35,2,1,talk,Mio,,The north rooms are freezing. We need a way to cover that extra heat.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The sub-metering quote is high. I need to see if it’s worth the upfront cost.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,The template I tried took hours. I don’t want to be the one doing that.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The monitors show one room uses four times the energy of another. That’s the issue.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,I saw a house that pays a fixed seasonal amount. No one argues about the switch.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi If one room uses so much, should they pay more? It feels unfair.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio It’s not about fairness, it’s about accuracy. But the quote is steep.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,@Shunichi I don’t want to be the one calculating that four times difference.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,@Rin I’ll do the math. I just need a method that reflects actual use.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,@Mio A fixed amount might stop the arguments. No one has to track the switch.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,I hate the idea of someone paying for my comfort. But I also hate the cold.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The payment log shows late payments when amounts changed. That’s a problem.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"If we use a template, I can do it, but it has to be simple. No hours of work.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,The statements show huge swings. A flat split is definitely wrong. We need data.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,The kitchen notice showed people avoiding the cooler to avoid the bill. That’s bad.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I think we need a base fee plus a usage fee. That way, no one is punished.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. But I need to know the exact cost of the meters before I commit.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,A base fee sounds good. But who calculates the usage part? I don’t want that job.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I can calculate it. I have the monitor data. Let’s propose a hybrid model.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,A hybrid model could work. It reduces the friction. I support looking into that.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
